From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:59:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Turn SMC detection off once Mono's backpatcher is found, as
 upstream

Madeira skipped DisableSMCDetection on iOS (ml648) because Mono's code pages
could not be made writable on the guest VA. Since madeira-unix 0019 that range
is the JIT pool's RW view and 0027 applies the write half of a protection
there, so the reprotect works. Without it every block compiled from a Mono
code page reprotects that page read-only, the next method Mono writes there
faults, and FEX invalidates the page and resets every thread's call-return
stack. MADEIRA_KEEP_SMC=1 keeps the tracking for an A/B.

Also count code invalidations by caller, with their cost, in an
[inv-census] line every 1024 invalidations.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-first-run-stutter.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp | 84 +++++++++++++++----
 Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.h   |  6 +-
 2 files changed, 74 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
